WF-30 — Payment Pending Handler

## Summary

- Purpose: Thin state handler for `payment_pending` user text. Classifies via WF-25 (which owns all safety actions), then does its one stage-specific job: a grounded Gemini reply (KB-bounded, topic-gated defer) for general enquiries, or a contextual payment reminder for other pass-through intents. Both customer replies are sent as INTERACTIVE messages that append a single canonical payment-details block and re-attach the [Payment Completed ✓] button. stop_intent needs no extra action (WF-25 already sent the clarifier); garbage / abuse terminate inside WF-25.
- Inputs (WF-01 canonical envelope §2.1, received via trigger passthrough): `phoneNumber` (top-level), `messageContent`, `user.{id, name, status, slack_channel_id}`. (The envelope carries no `messageText`/top-level `userId`/`userStatus` — those are read off `user.*` and `messageContent`.)
- Outputs: an interactive WhatsApp reply — for general_enquiry a grounded Gemini answer, for other pass-through a contextual reminder — each ending with the canonical payment-details block + a [Payment Completed ✓] button. No output for stop_intent / garbage / abuse (handled in WF-25).
- State Transitions: none.
- Calls Sub-Workflows: WF-25 (Intent Classifier + Safety-Net Hub), WF-53 (U1 — on the local Gemini reply's failure), WF-50 (Send WhatsApp).
- **Deltas vs the prior WF-30 (safety-net §6):**
  - REMOVED the inline Gemini-error halt-and-notify chain (~12 nodes) → on the general-reply Gemini failure, call U1 instead.
  - REMOVED the in-handler stop_intent clarifier (now sent by WF-25).
  - **PDF-04/05 (2026-06-06):** the general-enquiry Gemini reply is now grounded in a fixed business-facts KB with a topic-gated defer rule (no improvised services/pricing; personal astrology deferred to Dr. Chinmay). See Step 5.
  - **PDF-12 (2026-06-07):** payment instructions are a single CANONICAL block appended in code to BOTH the general-enquiry reply and the reminder; Gemini no longer phrases payment. Every payment_pending reply now shows identical, complete payment details.
  - **PDF-11 (2026-06-06):** both reply paths re-attach the [Payment Completed ✓] button (interactive message) so the user never scrolls back to the original payment message.
- **Notes:**
  - WF-25 returns `intentResult` only for pass-through and stop_intent; garbage / abuse do not continue here. **Mechanism (BUG-06c, safety-net §13):** on garbage/abuse WF-25 emits **0 items** (its Step 13 `Return Nothing`); this handler's `Call WF-25` has `alwaysOutputData=false`, so 0 items → Step 3 onward skip. A dead-end inside WF-25 alone does NOT stop this handler — before BUG-06c it returned 1 item and this handler wrongly sent the canned payment reminder on garbage. Do not remove WF-25's `Return Nothing`.
  - **Canonical payment block (single source):** the payment-details text (₹500 via GPay/PhonePe/UPI to the UPI payee, then "tap the button below to confirm") is one canonical block, byte-identical in the general-enquiry reply and the reminder, so payment instructions are consistent and complete on every reply. Gemini is explicitly told NOT to phrase payment (it may still state the ₹500 price if asked).
  - **Button re-attach:** the [Payment Completed ✓] reply button (stable id `payment_completed`) is re-sent on every reply; the id is unchanged so tapping it transitions payment_pending → payment_submitted exactly as the original button did (no router change).
  - Copy reuse-existing — verify verbatim at build.

---

## Algorithm

Step 1: Start — triggered by WF-02 with the WF-01 canonical envelope (trigger passthrough). Read `phoneNumber` from the top-level envelope field.
Step 2: Call WF-25 with `{ phoneNumber, userId: user.id, messageContent, userStatus: user.status, userName: user.name, slackChannelId: user.slack_channel_id }`. Receive `intentResult`. (If WF-25 hits a Gemini failure or handles garbage/abuse, it halts/terminates inside itself and control does not return here.)
Step 3: Check: `intentResult == 'stop_intent'`?
  - If YES → End (WF-25 already sent the clarifier; no stage-specific extra for payment_pending).
  - If NO → go to Step 4.
Step 4: Check: `intentResult == 'general_enquiry'`?
  - If YES → go to Step 5.
  - If NO → go to Step 7.
Step 5: Build a grounded Gemini prompt (gemini-2.5-flash-lite) for a brief, warm reply, bounded by a fixed business-facts KB and a topic-gated defer rule:
  - KB facts (the ONLY facts it may state): offering = a text-based Vedic astrology consultation over WhatsApp; ₹500 per consultation; each consultation covers ONE question/topic (may span several back-and-forth messages, Dr. Chinmay decides when answered); audio/video/automatic-payment are NOT available yet (coming soon); after a consultation closes, a new one is booked via REBOOK.
  - Response rule (pick one): greeting → warm reply; a question answerable from KB (price, what's offered, audio/video availability, how to book) → answer from KB only (audio/video → "coming soon, text-only for now"); a GENERIC/educational astrology question → may answer briefly; a question about THIS person (their chart/predictions/life questions, or remedies/gemstones/mantras for them) → do NOT answer, defer with exactly "That's something Dr. Chinmay will look into for you during your consultation."; off-topic → brief polite redirect.
  - The prompt MUST NOT phrase payment instructions or tell the user where/how to pay or to tap a button (it MAY state the ₹500 price) — payment details are appended deterministically in the next step.
  Append the user's message, then POST to Gemini. On Gemini failure → go to Step 6 (U1). On success → extract the reply (fallback: "Thank you for your message! For questions about our Vedic astrology consultation, feel free to ask."), then APPEND the canonical payment-details block (see Notes), and send via WF-50 as an INTERACTIVE message: body = reply + payment block, with one reply button [Payment Completed ✓] (id `payment_completed`). End.
Step 6: Gemini failure — call U1 with `{ phoneNumber, userFacing: true, consultChannelId: user.slack_channel_id, context: { source: 'WF-30', userName: user.name, userStateText: 'awaiting payment', userMessage: messageContent, errorDetail: <summary> } }` (apologise + alert + halt). End.
Step 7: Build a contextual payment reminder:
  - wants_consultation → prefix "Great! You're almost there. To confirm your consultation, please complete the payment below."
  - rebook_intent → prefix "For rebooking, please complete the pending payment first."
  - otherwise → prefix "Happy to help! Once your payment is confirmed, Dr. Chinmay will be ready for your consultation."
  - append the SAME canonical payment-details block used in Step 5: ₹500 via GPay/PhonePe/UPI to +91-9653240263 (Chinmay Mujumdar — the UPI payee/bank name), then "Once you've paid, tap the button below to confirm." (Note: the verbatim no longer says "the button you received earlier" — the button is re-sent on this message.)
  Send via WF-50 as an INTERACTIVE message: body = prefix + payment block, with one reply button [Payment Completed ✓] (id `payment_completed`). End.
